insert into public.budget_of_work (grade, subject, content_markdown, source_file)
values (
  6,
  'MAPEH',
  $bow$# Grade 6 MAPEH — Budget of Work

MAPEH is graded as two components — Music & Arts, and Physical Education & Health — each with its own quarterly grade that is then averaged. The Music & Arts sequence below follows the official Grade 6 curriculum guide (themed around Philippine history through Music and Arts); the PE & Health sequence extends the Grade 4 foundation with more advanced skills, since a full PE & Health source was not fetched this pass.

## Term 1: Music & Arts — Development in Music and Arts in the Revolutionary Period (1801-1898); PE & Health — Advanced Movement and Fitness
- **Music:** Timbre (instrumental ensembles, vocal styles/techniques) and dynamics (dynamic markings) as heard in sacred and secular vocal/instrumental music of the period; active listening, describing, and performing (singing, moving, playing).
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Relevant theater forms and their subjects/themes/symbolisms from the period, with focus on character and conflict; dance forms and their role in different time periods.
- **PE:** Demonstrating refined locomotor and manipulative skills in modified team games; applying rules and teamwork strategies.
- **Health:** Assessing personal fitness using simple tests and setting a personal fitness goal.

## Term 2: Music & Arts — Development of Philippine Music and Arts in the American Colonial Period (1898-1935); PE & Health — Team Games
- **Music:** Rhythm (meter, time signatures, rhythmic dance patterns) and tempo (musical symbols/terms for speed), drawn from Philippine classical, semi-classical, and popular music of the period.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Symbolic theater and seditious plays, focusing on dramatic structure; dance forms of the period and their role.
- **PE:** Organizing and participating in a small class tournament applying fair-play values.
- **Health:** Explaining puberty and adolescent changes in an age-appropriate way and the importance of hygiene during this stage.

## Term 3: Music & Arts — Development of Music and Arts during the Commonwealth Period and Japanese Occupation (1935-1946); PE & Health — Substance Abuse Awareness and First Aid
- **Music:** Melody (tonality/mode) and harmony (basic accompaniment), drawn from folk music relevant to the period and region; listening, creating, performing, evaluating.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Symbolic theater and seditious plays with focus on staging and spectacle; dance forms of the period.
- **Health:** Identifying risks of substance abuse (tobacco, alcohol) and strategies to resist peer pressure; practicing basic first-aid steps for minor injuries.

## Term 4: Music & Arts — "My Filipino Identity" (Contemporary Period); PE & Health — Year-End Showcase
- **Music:** Texture (monophony, homophony, polyphony, heterophony) and form (free-form, strophic, binary, ternary), in the context of the Philippine contemporary period; composing, performing, reflecting.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Performance practices in Philippine history that present and celebrate Filipino identities, applying elements of drama (character, plot, setting); dance forms focused on communicative function.
- **PE and Health:** A culminating physical activity showcase demonstrating fitness, teamwork, and healthy-living habits developed across the year.
- **Year-end project:** Produce a contemporary creative work (Music & Arts) depicting historical/cultural/national identity, using relevant concepts and practices from across the year, alongside a PE/Health showcase — together forming the MAPEH culmination for Key Stage 2.

**Special Science enrichment:** hindi inilalapat sa asignaturang MAPEH.$bow$,
